00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:22.576
Luckily for me, and
luckily for so many of us,

00:02:22.576 --> 00:02:25.645
we got to live during this
era where everything changes

00:02:25.645 --> 00:02:26.713
so much.

00:02:26.713 --> 00:02:30.484
I'm baffled by people not
understanding what happens

00:02:30.484 --> 00:02:33.787
when we move 
to a Snapchat universe,

00:02:33.787 --> 00:02:36.523
all the same shit that happened
on every other platform

00:02:36.523 --> 00:02:37.824
that had people's attention,

00:02:37.824 --> 00:02:41.194
whether it's print or radio,
television, or Facebook,

00:02:41.194 --> 00:02:45.399
so for me, thank God that
the markets gonna move

00:02:45.399 --> 00:02:49.603
on an everyday basis and
thank God people get old.

00:02:49.603 --> 00:02:51.405
And what I mean 
by people getting old

00:02:51.405 --> 00:02:54.174
is at South by Southwest 
it was funny.

00:02:54.174 --> 00:02:58.478
Chris Sacca exposed this thing
in his big Vanity Fair piece,

00:02:58.478 --> 00:02:59.713
which we make fun of,

00:02:59.713 --> 00:03:01.715
but for years we had 
this very small group

00:03:01.715 --> 00:03:04.117
that at South-by would get
together at like midnight

00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:06.353
and go in literally
just a small hotel room,

00:03:06.353 --> 00:03:08.655
