and we would basically,

00:03:08.655 --> 00:03:11.258
we called it the jam session, 
all it was was

00:03:11.258 --> 00:03:14.428
literally "Is Pinterest
worth a billion dollars?"

00:03:14.428 --> 00:03:16.363
"What do you think is
gonna happen with Uber?"

00:03:16.363 --> 00:03:17.764
and we did that for 
seven or eight years,

00:03:17.764 --> 00:03:19.332
it was really interesting
to see where people

00:03:19.332 --> 00:03:20.834
were right and wrong,

00:03:20.834 --> 00:03:23.270
and it was just amazing
debates and I learned so much.

00:03:23.270 --> 00:03:25.906
But to me the 
Q and A and the banter

00:03:25.906 --> 00:03:28.942
and the content 
is so imperative.

00:03:28.942 --> 00:03:31.812
It was two years ago at the
jam session where literally

00:03:31.812 --> 00:03:34.581
the founders, 
the founders of Twitter

00:03:34.581 --> 00:03:38.752
and Instagram and these
tools poo-poohed Snapchat.

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:43.090
And like just really, 
it was crazy.

00:03:43.090 --> 00:03:44.858
I was literally emphatically
yelling at them,

00:03:44.858 --> 00:03:48.228
like you guys changed
the world, and everybody

00:03:48.228 --> 00:03:50.363
said the same shit about
your product five years ago,

00:03:50.363 --> 00:03:51.965
how did you get so old so fast?

00:03:51.965 --> 00:03:52.966
(audience laughs)

00:03:52.966 --> 00:03:56.903
And so you know, obviously
whether it's entrepreneurship

00:03:56.903 --> 00:03:59.039
or investing or 
running a company,

00:03:59.039 --> 00:04:01.908
I think for the people here
that have had the time,

00:04:01.908 --> 00:04:03.743
'cause I know some 
of you are so busy,

00:04:03.743 --> 00:04:05.846
in the last six months to a
year I've been spending a lot

00:04:05.846 --> 00:04:10.083
more time on what really
has allowed me the privilege

00:04:10.083 --> 00:04:11.785
